<title>RUSSIA: RUSSIAN 182-DAY T-BILL YIELDS 18.97 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>RUSSIAN 182-DAY T-BILL YIELDS 18.97 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 182-day Russian GKO discount Treasury bills was 18.97 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield between 17.34 and 18.61 percent.</p>
<p>Series 23002 bills, maturing on February 18, 1998, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed at 91.20 on Tuesday, to yield 18.54 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		 21084</p>
<p>    Issue volume		  4.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		4.56 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		   4.15 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold			    3.70 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			3.38 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		 91.36 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price     91.21 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		 18.97 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield    19.33 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			   182 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		 Feb 11, 1998</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the Finance Ministry raised 4.99 trillion roubles at a previous auction of one-year T-bills, making total proceeds from today's auctions 8.37 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It has also repaid about 8.36 trillion roubles in a maturing 252-day series 22061 T-bill issue.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
